I'll admit: almost all the German I've heard in recent years has been
uttered by alternative musicians (mostly the bands Einstuerzende
Neubauten, Das Ich, and Rammstein), but from these, there definitely
seem to be two different ways to pronounce 'en', depending on where it
appears:

at the end of a word: usually with the 'e' being a schwa, as in "sie
mussen sich".
followed by another consonant: usually with the 'e' being stressed, as
in "unendlich" and "letztendlich".

Terminal 'e' preceded by a consonant seems to be almost always a schwa,
as in "hier kommt die Sonne".

(I'm perfectly prepared to believe that Blixa Bargeld and Till Lindemann
have appalling German diction; they are alternative musicians, after
all.)

